                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 45-year-old male, admitted on 06/08/2001 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with guarding. Laboratory investigations confirmed leukocytosis. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient underwent successful laparoscopic emergency appendectomy without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, intravenous fluids and analgesics were administered, and wound care was provided. Recovery was uneventful, with resolution of symptoms and normalization of inflammatory markers. The patient was mobilized early and discharged home on 09/08/2001 in good general condition. Please continue postoperative follow-up and wound monitoring. Should any complications arise, readmission is recommended promptly. Kind regards.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
